Package: liblol
Architecture: loong64
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: libstdc++6, libc6 (>= 2.36), libc6 (<< 2.43.1)
Recommends: liblol-dkms
Conflicts: glibc
Breaks: libcrypt1 (>= 1:4.5.2.1~)
Homepage: https://github.com/AOSC-Dev/liblol
Description: Compatibility layer for old world applications
 This package contains a Compatibility layer for old world
 applications on new world loongarch64 platform.
 .
 libLoL (LoongArch on LoongArch) provides a user-space runtime for
 applications designed for the old-world LoongArch ABI (Loongnix, UOS,
 etc.).  This package ships a patched GNU C Library built for the
 old-world ABI, installed below /usr/lib/loongarch64-debian-linux-gnuow/
 so that the old-world dynamic loader can pick it up.
 .
 The la_ow_syscall kernel module (packaged separately, e.g. as
 liblol-dkms) is required for old-world system call compatibility.
